unqlite
------------------------------------------
UnQLite is a in-process software library which implements a self-contained,
serverless, zero-configuration, transactional NoSQL database engine. UnQLite is
a document store database similar to MongoDB, Redis, CouchDB etc. as well a
standard Key/Value store similar to BerkeleyDB, LevelDB, etc.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libunqlite-devel-1.2.1-1bl1
  libunqlite1-1.2.1-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/symisc/unqlite

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/symisc/unqlite/archive/refs/tags/1.2.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack unqlite-1.2.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./unqlite-1.2.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/unqlite-1.2.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/unqlite-1.2.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libunqlite1-1.2.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libunqlite-devel-1.2.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(unqlite)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/unqlite.README
  /usr/share/doc/unqlite/CHANGELOG.md
  /usr/share/doc/unqlite/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/unqlite/README.md

(libunqlite1)
  /usr/bin/cygunqlite-1.dll

(libunqlite-devel)
  /usr/include/unqlite.h
  /usr/lib/libunqlite.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/unqlite.pc

